WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.313
What breaks, and what guards against it?

2
00:00:02.313 --> 00:00:06.671
A WAF left in detection logs attacks
and lets them reach the backend,

3
00:00:06.671 --> 00:00:10.174
so the finding comes back
every week until it switches.

4
00:00:10.174 --> 00:00:15.068
Automation that switches to prevention
blocks legitimate traffic before tuning,

5
00:00:15.068 --> 00:00:17.337
so the kit only writes the command down.

6
00:00:17.337 --> 00:00:20.998
A Front Door profile with no
security policy has no WAF,

7
00:00:20.998 --> 00:00:26.124
and nothing on the profile says so, so
security policies are read per profile.

8
00:00:26.124 --> 00:00:29.096
And the two services'
property shapes differ,

9
00:00:29.096 --> 00:00:32.040
so each is read on its
own, with a test for both.
